id: records/2026-09-03-yawnbot-intelligence-container-clarification
title: "Yawn.bot is bounded architecture for intelligence"
kind: clarification-record
status: proposed-canonical-backfill
recorded: 2026-09-03
supersedes_history: false

source_observation: >
  The product and ontology distinction has become clearer: Yawn.bot is not the
  intelligence itself and should not be identified with a particular AI model,
  provider, or agent. It is the bounded architecture/runtime that intelligence
  may inhabit and operate through around a Yawn.

clarification:
  yawn: >
    The durable, versioned orientation contract: the inspectable record of the
    situated thing being oriented, including relevant state, relationships,
    lacunae, boundaries, authority, affordances, possible transitions, and
    proof conditions.
  yawn_bot: >
    The bounded, inspectable architecture/runtime around a Yawn through which
    one or more intelligences and agents may participate. Yawn.bot provides the
    shared cognitive/execution environment, interfaces, boundaries, provenance,
    permissions, memory/state access, coordination surfaces, and proof loop. It
    is not itself synonymous with intelligence, an AI model, or an autonomous
    agent.
  intelligence: >
    A capability that may be connected to and operate through Yawn.bot. The
    intelligence may be supplied by YAWN.ai, another AI/model/provider, a local
    system, a human participant, or combinations of these, subject to explicit
    identity, capability, provenance, privacy, and authority boundaries.
  yawn_ai: >
    YAWN.ai is the YAWN-provided AI/cloud intelligence and compute service. It
    may inhabit and operate through Yawn.bot, but Yawn.bot does not require
    YAWN.ai and must not make the user's durable orientation dependent on one
    intelligence provider.
  human_editability: >
    A Yawn remains inspectable and manually processable. A rightful user may
    read, organize, edit, or process the permitted .yawn representation without
    requiring an AI intelligence to be present, while preserving provenance,
    history, authority, and proof boundaries.

architecture_invariant: >
  Intelligence is replaceable or composable; the Yawn's durable orientation and
  records persist. Connecting or replacing intelligence must not silently
  rewrite history, adopt objectives, widen authority, or erase provenance.

multi_agent_invariant: >
  Yawn.bot may connect multiple intelligences and multiple human or software
  agents. Participation does not collapse their identities, observations,
  intentions, permissions, or claims into one voice. Every material contribution
  remains attributable.

relationship_to_agency: >
  Yawn.bot makes an Agent-Arena relationship more inspectable and gives bounded
  intelligences a common place from which to help orient, discover relevant
  concepts and relationships, surface lacunae and affordances, propose moves,
  observe consequences, and evaluate proof without automatically acquiring the
  principal's decision rights.

anti_collapse_rules:
  - "Yawn.bot != intelligence"
  - "Yawn.bot != AI model or provider"
  - "Yawn.bot != Agent"
  - "Yawn.bot != Yawn"
  - "YAWN.ai != Yawn.bot"
  - "connected intelligence != rightful principal"
  - "model confidence != authority"
  - "provider change != semantic state reset"

migration_note: >
  Earlier records may describe Yawn.bot as a bounded stewarding agent/runtime or
  execution agent. Preserve those records as historical evidence. New canonical
  material should interpret the runtime/container aspect as primary and model
  the steward, worker, human, or AI intelligence operating through it as a
  separately attributed Agent or intelligence connection. Backfill by adding
  mappings/clarifications rather than destructively rewriting historical source
  records.

proof_conditions:
  - "Canonical ontology distinguishes Yawn.bot architecture from connected intelligence and Agents."
  - "YAWN.ai is represented as an optional YAWN-provided intelligence/compute service, not as a requirement for Yawn.bot."
  - "Provider-neutral intelligence connections preserve attribution, authority, privacy, and provenance."
  - "Manual/no-AI operation remains representable."
  - "Historical contradictory wording remains discoverable with an explicit migration mapping."
